Description: Calculates heat-stress indices from meteorological observations
    using shared psychrometric calculations and consistent method-specific
    input handling. Methods include the physically based outdoor wet-bulb
    globe temperature model described by Liljegren et al. (2008)
    <doi:10.1080/15459620802310770>, wet-bulb temperature and heat-index
    calculations, and established closed-form heat-stress indices. Provides
    row-level diagnostics, configurable physical controls, vectorized batch
    processing, and optional parallel execution for the Liljegren method.
    It is an independently maintained fork of 'HeatStress'; its Liljegren
    implementation is not a bitwise-compatible port of the original program.
